  "interpretation": "<h3 data-start=\"1324\" data-end=\"1349\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\"><strong data-start=\"1328\" data-end=\"1347\">Interpretation:</strong></span></h3>\n<ul data-start=\"1350\" data-end=\"1642\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\" data-start=\"1350\" data-end=\"1445\">\n<p data-start=\"1352\" data-end=\"1445\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\"><strong data-start=\"1352\" data-end=\"1363\">Normal:</strong> No significant decrement (&le;10%) in CMAP amplitude after repetitive stimulation.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\" data-start=\"1446\" data-end=\"1564\">\n<p data-start=\"1448\" data-end=\"1564\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\"><strong data-start=\"1448\" data-end=\"1461\">Abnormal:</strong> &gt;10% decrement in CMAP amplitude suggests neuromuscular junction disorder (e.g., Myasthenia Gravis).</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\" data-start=\"1565\" data-end=\"1642\">\n<p data-start=\"1567\" data-end=\"1642\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\">Post-exercise increments may indicate presynaptic disorders (e.g., LEMS).</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
